OL,3,GNEWSACountry park wildfire damage still
OL,4,Abeing assessed
OL,5,
OL,6,FMore than a week on from a huge
OL,7,Fwildfire at a country park, the scale
OL,8,Fof devastation is still being assessed
OL,9,Fwith grassland and wildlife habitats
OL,10,Fseverely affected.
OL,12,FNo cause has yet been identified for
OL,13,Fthe fire which ripped through more than
OL,14,F50 acres of Mincinglake Valley Park on
OL,15,Fthe edge of Exeter on 11 August
OL,16,Fprompting the call out of 20 fire
OL,17,Fcrews.
OL,23,APub: 19-AugQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBW-SW Eng NewsC Reg TVFWeather
FL,346,340,200,160,0,100
PN,34502
SC,0002
CT,3,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F345A1787172967
OL,1,W5j 5Q555pjsjjj js17kjc15 js57kj#4
OL,2,W//%*// //%Q--% (.*.. *,$%**,%-,* %%**,!
OL,3,GNEWSACountry park wildfire damage still
OL,4,Abeing assessed
OL,5,
OL,6,FDevon Wildlife Trust, which manages the
OL,7,Fpark, said habitats had been destroyed
OL,8,Fby the fire which engulfed large areas
OL,9,Fof grassland and asked the public to
OL,10,Favoid badly burnt areas of the site.
OL,12,FThe trust said nature could be
OL,13,Fresilient and hoped that given time,
OL,14,Fthe area could "once again be a
OL,15,Fthriving wildlife-rich area".
OL,23,APub: 19-AugQppppppppppppppppppppppG2/2
